course: dictionary
lesson: 1096
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Brain» can name the organ inside your head, and it can also mean cleverness, or a very clever person. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «You smell cookies baking from the other room because tiny invisible bits have floated up your nose and landed on smell cells that tell your brain «cookies!».» Here the brain is the part of your body that receives messages. Try the meaning in the sentence: does it fit? Yes, so you have found the right one.
explain: «Use your brain» means think harder, so brain means cleverness here. «She's the brains of the team» means she is the clever one. Always read the words around the word before you decide what it means.
explain: Some words appear in phrases, and a phrase can have its own meaning. A brain teaser is a puzzle that makes you think. Brainstorm means thinking of lots of ideas together. Check the whole group of words, not just one.
fact: Brain means the organ inside your head that controls your body, thinking, memory and feelings.
fact: Brain can also mean cleverness, as in «Use your brain.»
fact: A very clever person can be called «the brains» of a team.
fact: In informal speech, «brain» can also mean to hit someone on the head.
fact: Your brain sends and receives messages through nerves, and sleep and healthy food help it work.
exercise: «Use your brain to solve this puzzle.» In this sentence, brain means: | A sweet cake | A soft grey organ inside a head | *Cleverness, thinking well | A sharp hit on the head
exercise: «You smell cookies because smell cells tell your brain «cookies!».» In this sentence, brain means: | *The organ inside your head that receives messages | A puzzle | A very clever person | Cleverness
exercise: Which phrase names a puzzle that makes you think? | brainstorm | *brain teaser | brainy | brain freeze
test: «She's the brains of the team.» Brains here means: | Lots of ideas | To hit on the head | The organ inside your head | *A very clever person
test: Which phrase means a sudden headache from eating something cold too fast? | brain teaser | *brain freeze | brainstorm | brainy
exam: «Animation is a lovely trick on your brain.» Brain here means: | To hit on the head | *The organ inside your head that takes in pictures and makes sense of them | Cleverness | A very clever person
